BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:We Live Here
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261219
DTSTAMP:20261116T204745Z
UID:561fc4d7ef1ba7afe9fe435470b7@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:An exhibition that looks at housing as the framework of commun
 ity life. With historical images\, photography\, architectural designs\, r
 esident testimony\, and interactive displays\, We Live Here will place a c
 entury of residential life in the greater New London area and Connecticut 
 in the broader context of the nation. The history of dwelling is our socia
 l history. It illuminates how our communities live now and could live bett
 er in the future.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/we-live-here
LOCATION:The Garde Gallery\, Garde Arts Center\, 305 State Street\, New Lo
 ndon CT\, 06320
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/we-live-here
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exhibition: Beyond the Ideal: Landscape\, Likeness\, & Belonging i
 n the 19th Century
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20290101
DTSTAMP:20261116T204745Z
UID:cb4d5fec2860add22defb9e5eccd@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of the 250th Anniversary of American Independen
 ce\, Slater Memorial Museum is pleased to present Beyond the Ideal: Landsc
 ape\, Likeness\, & Belonging in the 19th Century. This showcase of 19th-ce
 ntury American works explores how artists used landscapes\, portraits\, an
 d still lifes to articulate identity\, belonging\, and sense of place. The
  show will primarily focus on qualities of the Hudson River School movemen
 t and how local artists experimented with depicting traditional New Englan
 d scenes.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/exhibition-beyond-ideal-la
 ndscape-likeness-belonging-19th-century
LOCATION:Gualtieri Gallery\, Slater Memorial Museum\, 108 Crescent Street
 \, Norwich CT\, 06360
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/exhibition-beyond-ideal-landscape-likeness-
 belonging-19th-century
END:VEVENT
